/// mlrepro-generic-variant-closure-result-element-strands-var-heap-unbox-invalid-wasm.cdz
///
/// v-inference ROOT-CAUSED 2026-07-20 (from v-iterators' I1 re-probe note + the filed witness
/// issues/mlrepro-generic-state-var-adapter-erased-scalar-heap-abi.cdz). This is the p6 face:
/// a fully-generic adapter iterator `Mk(s, s -> Option((a, s)))` with a HEAP element (String)
/// emits INVALID WASM (`expected i32 found i64` at the failing function) even though `cdz check`
/// passes. p1 (Int element) passes only BY LUCK (see below).
///
/// ============================== ROOT CAUSE (confirmed) ==============================
/// The step closure's result tuple `(x, s)` monomorphizes to type `(Tuple _ (List String))`:
/// the STATE element grounds to `(List String)` but the PAYLOAD element `a` (node = the tuple's
/// Elem(0), i.e. `x`) STAYS an unresolved `Ty::Var (_)`. Verified via a get_op trace on the real
/// repro:
///   [getop] node=105 ty=_                     core=SumPayload { scrutinee: 98, path:[Elem(0)] }   ← x
///   [getop] node=98  ty=(Tuple _ (List String)) core=SumPayload { scrutinee: 90, path:[Payload] } ← (x,s)
///
/// At EMIT, `get_op_ty` (backend/wasm/select.rs ~2010) grounds a `Ty::Var | Ty::Any` projection to
/// `OP_GET_INT` (the i64 "dead-phantom-position" default). But here the read is LIVE: `x` is a String
/// HANDLE (i32) at this monomorphization. `get-int` yields an i64 → the downstream `value-eq` (which
/// wants an i32 handle) fails wasm validation with `expected i32 found i64`.
///
/// THE BOX/UNBOX ASYMMETRY: when the tuple `(h, t)` is BUILT, `box_op(db, h)` reads `h`'s OWN node
/// type = `String` (h binds the list head of a `List String`) → stores the String handle AS-IS (i32).
/// When it is READ, `get_op` reads the PROJECTION SLOT's type = `_` → `get-int` (i64). Box stored i32,
/// unbox reads i64 → mismatch. The box side already has a targeted safety net for the dual bug
/// (`box_op_for` / `node_produces_heap_handle`, the func[27] freeze fix) — it stores a Var-typed LIVE
/// HANDLE as-is instead of box-int'ing it. The UNBOX side has no such net, and CANNOT get one locally:
/// at a `Proj` we read from a heap slot and cannot see the producing node, so we can't tell a
/// handle-slot from a boxed-scalar-slot. ⇒ the fix must GROUND the element type var, not patch emit.
///
/// WHY p1 (Int) PASSES: `get-int` (i64) happens to match how an Int element is boxed (box-int, i64),
/// AND the `== 1` (scalar rhs) routes to `Core::Compare` (scalar), so the i64 lines up end-to-end. It
/// is accidental — the SAME element-var stranding, masked because get-int is right for a scalar Int.
///
/// TRIGGER AXIS (from v-iterators' matrix, all CHECK clean, fail at lowering/emit):
///   fully-generic + Int elem       → PASS (get-int matches box-int; accidental)
///   fully-generic + STRING elem    → invalid wasm `expected i32 found i64`  ← THIS repro
///   generic state + Int elem       → PASS (accidental)
///   generic state + STRING elem    → runtime `unreachable`
///   CONCRETE state + generic elem  → PASS (element grounds when state is concrete)
///   fully-generic + re-wrap closure→ "closure param has no machine representation"
///
/// DISTINCT from the recursive-generic DRIVER tie (parked) and the transformer-closure tie (fixed):
/// NONE of these recurse. It is the NON-recursive generic-variant-stored-closure RESULT-ELEMENT tie —
/// the element var of a closure result reached through a generic variant payload never grounds from
/// the concrete construction, while the STATE var does. A direct (non-adapter) head-into-tuple
/// (`match xs [h,..t] => Some((h,t))`) GROUNDS h fine and PASSES — the stranding is specific to the
/// value flowing through the `Mk(s, step)` variant + closure boundary (`step(s)` result element).
///
/// FIX DIRECTION (deep, unhurried — hot-path, regression-risky): ground the closure-result payload
/// element var from the concrete step argument at the generic-variant monomorphization (the state var
/// already grounds this way — make the element var do the same). Locus is the scheme/monomorphization
/// tie for a closure param whose Option/tuple RESULT mentions the payload var, adjacent to the
/// solved_lambda_arrow_under / apply_scheme_to_args family. Sibling of
/// [[scalar-eq-against-erased-type-param-value-mislowers-to-heap-value-eq]] but that was a COMPARE
/// routing fix; this strands the element TYPE itself, so a route-at-compare fix does not reach it.
///
/// The `@test` below reproduces the invalid wasm (compile fails at the step function). Kept as a
/// DECLINE/miscompile witness; flips to a run (unit) when the element-var tie lands.

type Iter =
  | Mk(s, s -> Option((a, s)))

def from-list(xs) = Iter.Mk(xs, fn(s) => match s with
  | [] => Option.None(unit)
  | [h, .. t] => Option.Some((h, t)))

def step-once(it) = match it with
  | Iter.Mk(s, step) => step(s)

@test
def p6-generic-string-step() =
  match step-once(from-list(["a", "b"])) with
  | Option.Some(p) => (match p with | (x, _) => if x == "a" then unit else trap("p6"))
  | Option.None(_) => trap("p6 none")
